From 688dd4a138dcac71d2d59ffccabe4e1546a01b1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:54:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Game screen: the task line, the timer at its end, the
 verdict and streak beside Next

- The row over the question goes: its category chip said what the
  tooltip's base line says. "Name this item" / "Pick the art that matches
  the name" is the turn's second line under the banner (the cards screen's
  prompt line), with the timer at its right end; whoever can't answer is
  told who is answering.
- At the reveal the verdict chip leads the result row beside Next. From
  three in a row it says "N in a row" instead of its word and burns with
  the scoreboard's own fire at the same tier (taken once per question).
- Turns mode: on someone else's turn the answers go grey and flat in place
  (frames, numbers and pictures kept), lighting up when your turn comes.
- Art question: the name is the heading (larger plate, one line where it
  fits, category under it); tall art in one row of tall tiles (host sends
  `tall`); the number above the art; the name at the reveal over the
  tile's foot.
- Long lists (Eternal's eight, Delve's eight and ten) in two columns beside
  the art; short desktop windows (up to 820 tall) tighten so every answer
  and Next fit; picture rows share the height there is.
- Phones: Detonate docked at the foot while dynamite is at hand; ten
  pictures two to a row; the result bar keeps the lower of your pick and
  the right answer in view; the docked chip keeps a streak's count.
- NamePlate `fit`: its ends sized to the plate, so the frame's rules sit on
  its edges at any height; the two ends meet at the middle.
- Tests for tall art (tests/tallArt.test.ts); the lab can set a streak.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
